2. Add a previous-leaf link

Your leaves currently only contain:

private LeafNode nextLeaf;

For forward range scans, nextLeaf is enough. However, your project notes mention sibling links, and a complete implementation can also add:

private LeafNode previousLeaf;

This becomes useful for reverse scans and deletion rebalancing.

3. Add a tree integrity verifier

You have some internal validation code, but there is no public tree-level verifier that checks:

- keys are sorted;
- every internal node has the correct number of children;
- all leaves are at the same depth;
- parent separators route keys correctly;
- leaf links are ordered and complete;
- no entries are lost or duplicated.

This is strongly recommended before moving to disk storage.

4. Add more structural tests

Your existing tests cover insertion, leaf splits, internal splits, root replacement, range scans, and randomized insertion/search. Add tests for:

